A/B: split the single UBI `fit` volume into `fit-a`/`fit-b` and add
/chosen rootdisk-spim-nand-a/-b phandles (openwrt-one, mt7981b, Track B).

NAND-only board: A/B lives in UBI, not GPT. The kernel binds the root
block device by matching a ubiblock's parent (UBI volume) of_node against
the /chosen/rootdisk phandle (drivers/mtd/ubi/vmt.c find_volume_fwnode
sets vol->dev of_node from the DT volname; drivers/block fitblk matches it).
So two volumes fit-a/fit-b each get their own DT node, and u-boot's
mt7981 ft_system_setup (z03) repoints /chosen/rootdisk to the active slot.

Static `rootdisk` and plain `rootdisk-spim-nand` both default to fit-a so an
un-patched u-boot / unset active_slot still boots slot A, matching z03's
fallback. volname uses hyphens (fit-a/fit-b) per existing DTS convention.

Two separate hunks (the /chosen and volumes nodes are ~300 lines apart);
applied via `git apply` whose --check fails loudly, so no silent-drop risk.

diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7981b-openwrt-one.dts b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7981b-openwrt-one.dts
